    {
      "table": "6.11-loop",
      "position": 2,
      "ids": [
        "toolkit.createGoals"
      ],
      "cells": [
        "`create-goals [--brief \\| --brief-file \\| --from-stdin \\| positional text] [--codex-goal-mode aggregate\\|per_story] [--validation-batch-json] [--force]`",
        "`createGoals({ brief, codexGoalMode?, validationBatchesJson?, force? })`. The brief has four sources that all fill the one `brief` field, taken in this order: `--brief`, then the file of `--brief-file`, then stdin with `--from-stdin`, then the positional words not consumed by a flag, joined by spaces. A brief that is empty after that is refused `ULW_LOOP_BRIEF_REQUIRED` (`cli-subcommands.ts:29-41`, `cli-arg-parser.ts:44-54`). The order and the refusal are the descriptor's parse, pinned by scenarios. The parser also accepts `--after-json`, `--directive-json`, `--directive-file` and `--target-goal-id` (`cli-arg-parser.ts:8`) only to keep their values out of the positional brief; nothing reads them. They are adapter parse flags with no SDK input and the written reason \"its value is removed from the positional brief; nothing reads it\", with one scenario that shows the brief excludes the value",
        "same"
      ]
    },
